    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="1737" n="1721" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.022/6–851</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of Embassy in Argentina</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Martindale</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-06-08">June 8, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 1923</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Argentine Reply to British Protest Concerning
                    Antarctic Bases.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d764-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Foreign Minister<anchor n="2" xml:id="d764-f2"/> received the press on June 7
                    and issued copies of the note handed British Embassy June 1<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d764-f3"/> rejecting the British protest against Argentine bases
                    established in Antarctica. (Clippings from <hi rendition="#italic">La
                        Nación</hi>, June 8, <hi rendition="#italic">Democracia</hi>, June 8 and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Epoca</hi>, June 7, enclosed.)<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d764-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Peronista press headlines the government’s strong nationalist stand and
                    reassertion of Argentine sovereignty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> G. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Martindale</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d764-f1" n="1" xml:id="d764-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch 1753, from Buenos Aires, May 10, not printed, had reported that the
                    British Embassy had formally protested against the establishment of two more
                    Argentine bases in Antarctica (735.00 (W)/5–1051).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f2" n="2" xml:id="d764-f2-content">
                <p>Argentine Foreign Minister Dr. Hipolito J. Paz.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f3" n="3" xml:id="d764-f3-content">
                <p>The text of the note was enclosed with despatch 1977, from Buenos Aires, June 18,
                    not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f4" n="4" xml:id="d764-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
